The latest changes need to be adapted for the Windows version, and how the
Windows uninstaller manages to delete itself still needs finalizing.

The problem on Windows is that, unlike on Linux, files in use by a running program (including the program itself) cannot be deleted. It might be functionally neatest to use a Powershell script for the uninstaller, as this can delete itself (I think ...), but that means a whole new program in a different language with a different GUI. Especially the translations look challenging.

At present the compromise solution is probably to use a simple Powershell script to copy the uninstaller (with libraries) to a temporary location, run the uninstaller, then finally delete the temporary stuff. The current C++ uninstaller has code for copying itself, which might be more convenient than copying in Powershell.

